                                    </div>

                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>What are India ASCI rules for skincare before-after?</h3>
                                        <p>Same person + same conditions + reasonable time-frame + clinical/consumer study substantiation required. No cure claims. Disclaimer language. ASCI complaints trigger 15-day response window + takedown if non-compliant.</p>
                                        <h3>What are GCC ESMA + SFDA rules for skincare advertising?</h3>
                                        <p>ESMA UAE requires cosmetic notification + substantiation. SFDA Saudi requires prior approval + halal + culturally-conservative model imagery. Both stricter than India ASCI on substantiation + imagery.</p>
                                        <h3>Can we use dramatic before-after skincare imagery?</h3>
                                        <p>No. Dramatic + implied cure before-after triggers ASCI + ESMA + SFDA takedowns. Use real consumer + real timeline + substantiated language + disclaimer. Substantiated specifics convert better than vague absolute claims.</p>
                                        <h3>Do we need a clinical study for skincare claims?</h3>
                                        <p>Consumer study (N=30-60 + 4-8 weeks + self-perception) at Rs 2-5 lakh minimum. Clinical study (N=30-50 + 4-12 weeks + instrumental measurement) for scientific claims + Rs 5-15 lakh. One-time investment per SKU + amortised across ad + landing + PR for 12-24 months.</p>
                                        <h3>What language is safe for skincare advertising?</h3>
                                        <p>"Helps address" instead of "reduces". "Supports" instead of "removes". "Age-defence" instead of "anti-aging". "Visible improvement in 2-8 weeks" instead of "instant". "Consumer-study substantiated" instead of "clinical proof".</p>
                                        <h3>What disclaimers must skincare before-after include?</h3>
                                        <p>"Individual results may vary based on skin type + lifestyle + adherence." "Based on X-week consumer study of N subjects." "Results shown are typical of study participants." Placement: visible on ad + landing page + product page.</p>
                                        <h3>Can we use real customer testimonials?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes with signed release + real product usage + real timeline. Paid testimonials require disclosure (#Ad #Paid). Genuine customer + genuine before-after strongest converting format when compliance-safe.</p>
                                        <h3>How does ITD GrowthLabs handle skincare compliance + before-after?</h3>
                                        <p>Compliance advisor + claims review + substantiation study coordination + ASCI + ESMA + SFDA advertising rules + safe-language creative production. Every creative reviewed for claim-legality before publish. See <a href="/industries/digital-marketing-for-skincare-brands.php">skincare vertical page</a>.</p>
